    "segments": [
      {
        "id": "09",
        "text": "With the problem framed, we turn to data. Data earns trust only after it is qualified for a specific use. A file that opens, a chart that looks right, a promising model signal: none of them alone establishes meaning, quality, permission, or reproducibility. So ask six questions. Where did it come from? When was it knowable? What does it mean? What changed it? How good is it? And how may it be used? Data that cannot answer them may be explored within its authorized scope, but stays out of shared, production and decision work until qualified. Reports, catalogs, cached copies and Agent summaries are secondary sources. None may quietly become the source of truth.",
